    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557">

                <pb facs="0980" n="876" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg876"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d557-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-03-04">4 March 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>601. Prime Minister to President Roosevelt
                    personal and most secret.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>About the Italian ships et cetera. I was much startled by the press accounts of
                    your talk with them. The Russians have never asked for <pb facs="0981" n="877"
                        xml:id="pg877"/> one-third of the Italian ships, but only for the specific
                    vessels mentioned at Moscow and agreed to by us at Teheran. See list which
                    follows. We have never agreed, as you know, to anything beyond this.…</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d557-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d557-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Military Attaché, London, via Army channels.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
